event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":94,"item_id":"rs_0c96195ccc6f49a8016acd305420b48195b5d09c708606aaf3","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering validator implementation**\n\nI'm working on implementing a validator object that isn't an array and is required based on type. I'm thinking about the version being equal to 1, and whether to override any blank precedences. There seems to be some complexity around existing import sizes and limits, like a 64k cap, but I want to ensure practicality. I could allow imports beyond that, like up to 16MB, while keeping existing caps optional. Normalizing different parameters seems useful too."}

